113 069** byte-for-byte\nC-vs-Rust comparisons (counter reported by the harness at process exit, not an\nestimate). Combined with Phase C: **116 870** total differential comparisons.\n\nAll 30 rows pass under all six build configurations:\n\n| profile | features | phase B | phase C | phase D |\n|---------|----------|---------|---------|---------|\n| debug   | `<default>` | 30/30 | 7/7 | 2/2 |\n| debug   | `--no-default-features` | 30/30 | 7/7 | 2/2 |\n| debug   | `--all-features` | 30/30 | 7/7 | 2/2 |\n| release | `<default>` | 30/30 | 7/7 | 2/2 |\n| release | `--no-default-features` | 30/30 | 7/7 | 2/2 |\n| release | `--all-features` | 30/30 | 7/7 | 2/2 |\n\nThe **debug** rows matter independently: `debug-assertions`/`overflow-checks`\nare ON there, so they prove none of the translated arithmetic\n(`l += 1`, `k += 4`, `b1 << 2`, `strlen + 1`) overflows or panics where the C\nsilently wraps.\n\nReproduce everything with `./run_all_checks.sh`.\n\n## Harness sensitivity (mutation check)\n\nTo prove the suite is not vacuously green, eight single-token mutations were\ninjected into `src/lib.rs` one at a time; **every one was killed**:\n\n| mutation | tests failed |\n|----------|--------------|\n| `decode('+')` returns 61 instead of 62 | 25 |\n| `is_base64` no longer accepts `'='` | 27 |\n| `c3 != '='` padding check altered | 27 |\n| empty-string guard (`*src != 0`) removed | 27 |\n| `k += 4` → `k += 3` | 30 |\n| `calloc` size `l + 13` → `l + 12` | 30 |\n| `b2 >> 4` → `b2 >> 3` | 30 |\n| `b3 & 0x3` → `b3 & 0x7` | 30 |\n\n`src/lib.rs` was then restored and byte-diffed against the original (identical).\nEOF\nwc -l SYMBOLS.md ERRORS.md CONFIGS.md","description":"Append verification results to artifacts"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":459,"cache_read_input_tokens":72542,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":459,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"stand