comparison is over the full `strlen+14` allocation, not `strcmp`.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n1. **The suite was validated, not just run.** All tests passed on the first attempt, which is exactly when a harness deserves suspicion. I injected 20 single-token mutations into `src/lib.rs` one at a time (md5-verified restore between each): **18 killed** (4–29 tests each). The 2 survivors (`b2 & 0xf` → `0x1f`, `b3 & 0x3` → `0x7`) are **provably equivalent** — the extra mask bit lands in bit 8 and is discarded by `as u8`; proven by exhaustive enumeration over `decode()`'s full `0..=63` domain, 0 counterexamples. So they are dead mask bits, not coverage gaps.\n2. **A mid-session process error, now corrected.** `$TMPDIR` changes between tool calls, so my first mutation batch silently failed to restore between runs and applied all 8 mutations *cumulatively*, leaving `src/lib.rs` corrupted with no backup. I reverted it with exact-match edits and byte-diffed it against the original recorded in context (identical). I then re-ran the mutation study correctly with an in-workdir backup — the table in `CONFIGS.md` reflects the accurate one-at-a-time data, not the invalid first run.\n\nTwo caveats on scope: `ERRORS.md` rows 3–4 are `calloc`/`malloc` failure paths, unreachable on a 64-bit host with overcommit — covered structurally (NULL/non-NULL verdict identical over 4,000 inputs incl. 1 MiB, same allocation order and `free(dest)` cleanup) rather than by induced OOM. And `int l = strlen(src) + 1` truncation only bites above 2 GiB; the wrapping semantics are replicated via `wrapping_add`, but not exercised at that size.\n\nArtifacts: `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`, `tests/{common/mod.rs,phase_b_configs.rs,phase_c_errors.rs,phase_d_symbols.rs}`, and `run_all_checks.sh` (reproduces everything). `c_src/` sources untouched. Note that `cargo` needs `--offline` here — crates.io is blocked by the proxy, and `libloading 0.8.9` came from the local cache."}],"stop_reason":null,